{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["And Jacob came shalem — to a city whose name is Shalem. As in: ״ותבאנה בית לחם״." "The city of Shechem — the city of Shechem, as in: ״כי חשבון עיר סיחון מלך האמרי היא״, as it is written: ״וירא אותה שכם בן חמור החוי״. And the one who explains that Shechem is the name of the city is mistaken, for nowhere do we find 'the city of Zion,' 'Jerusalem' — rather, the word 'city' appears after the name. And even if this is indeed Shechem, perhaps they named the city Shechem in memory of the valor of Jacob's sons, as it is written of Luz, which was called Beth-El, and as it is written: ״ויקראו ללשם דן על שם דן אביהם״ — in memory of their valor, that they killed the men of the city, and as it is written: ״והוא היה בונה עיר ויקרא שם העיר כשם בנו חנוך״. And also the one who explains 'shalem' as 'whole in his Torah, whole in his wealth' is mistaken according to the plain sense, for it is not the way of Scripture to speak thus. And furthermore, what need is there — was it really for the sake of a modest gift that he gave Esau that this needed to be written?!"], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:46:11.772913055Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}